      "content": "wait, you said in your first response that expanding privilege is an \"endangering erosion,\" but then in this second part you're saying the \"strongest argument\" involves the fact that congressional investigations are \"often partisan and overreaching.\" \n\ndoesn't that basically mean the \"erosion\" argument is actually weaker if we acknowledge that Congress uses its oversight power as a political weapon? if the investigations themselves are the problem, doesn't that make the expansion of privilege the more legally sound solution for protecting the office? just be real with me, which one actually holds up better in a modern court?",
